WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:03.569
-Despite
the multitasking involved

00:00:03.569 --> 00:00:04.837
with being the president,

00:00:04.837 --> 00:00:06.005
Trump still finds a way

00:00:06.005 --> 00:00:08.340
to enrich himself
and his family financially,

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.009
so, today we wanted to check in

00:00:10.009 --> 00:00:11.878
on one particularly
insidious way

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:14.280
Trump and us his family have
been profiting, specifically,

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.482
from a policy
that was supposed to benefit

00:00:16.482 --> 00:00:19.318
the low-income communities
Trump promised to help.

00:00:19.318 --> 00:00:20.753
This is "The Check In."

00:00:20.753 --> 00:00:23.055
[ Cheering and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:23.055 --> 00:00:25.224
[ Ding ding ]

00:00:25.224 --> 00:00:28.728
When then-candidate Trump was
campaigning for the presidency,

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:31.430
back when the words
"President Trump" sounded like

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:34.333
one of those silly oxymorons,
like jumbo shrimp

00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:36.569
or moderate Republican,

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:38.071
[ Laughter ]
he was promising to help

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:39.672
America's
impoverished communities

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:42.041
and he did it in the only way
Donald Trump knows how:

00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:43.976
by insulting the very people

00:00:43.976 --> 00:00:46.146
he was trying to convince
to vote for him.

00:00:46.146 --> 00:00:49.649
-Look how much
African American communities

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:53.920
have suffered
under Democratic control.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:57.956
To those, I say the following:

00:00:57.956 --> 00:01:00.860
What do you have to lose?

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.394
Look, what do you have to lose?

00:01:02.394 --> 00:01:04.296
You're living in poverty.

00:01:04.296 --> 00:01:05.765
Your schools are no good.

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:07.901
You have no jobs.

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:11.204
58% of your youth is unemployed.

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:12.805
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.805 --> 00:01:15.575
What the hell
do you have to lose?

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:17.677
[ Laughter ]
-Jesus!

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:19.646
He tried to sell his policies

00:01:19.646 --> 00:01:22.214
the same way drug dealers
try to sell meth.

00:01:22.214 --> 00:01:24.884
[ Laughter ]
"Look, you're livin' in poverty.

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:26.820
You got no job,
why not let crystal

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.088
take the wheel for a while?

00:01:29.088 --> 00:01:30.289
[ Laughter ]
Whaddya got to lose?"

00:01:30.289 --> 00:01:33.059
Trump actually instituted
a policy which he claimed

00:01:33.059 --> 00:01:34.526
was specifically meant
to build up

00:01:34.526 --> 00:01:36.495
America's abandon cities
and towns.

00:01:36.495 --> 00:01:39.232
Tucked away in the unpopular
GOP tax bill

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:41.568
was a specific tax benefit
referred to

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:44.203
as opportunity zones,
which sounds like

00:01:44.203 --> 00:01:46.372 line:0%
a weird sex manual
from the '70s, you know.

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:48.174 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
"Things were dead in the bed

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:50.109
with Barb and I, but after I
found her opportunity zone,

00:01:50.109 --> 00:01:52.111
it's a whole other story."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.111 --> 00:01:53.913
Trump's tax bill contained
an incentive

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:56.616
that allows investors
to delay paying taxes

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:58.651
if they agree to invest money

00:01:58.651 --> 00:01:59.952
into an area
that desperately needs it,

00:01:59.952 --> 00:02:02.488
or, as it's known,
an opportunity zone.

00:02:02.488 --> 00:02:04.290
In theory,
it sounds like a good idea.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.459
Distressed communities need
better schools and housing,

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:07.493
and that requires money.

00:02:07.493 --> 00:02:08.861
Investors are hesitant

00:02:08.861 --> 00:02:10.930
to pour cash into areas
that may not turn a profit,

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:13.032
so the administration
is offering benefits

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:14.267
for them to take that risk.

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:16.668
But the problem
with opportunity zones is

00:02:16.668 --> 00:02:19.672
that only one of those promises
has been fulfilled:

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:22.041
The one where wealthy people
made even more money.

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:23.309
Reports show that the...

00:02:31.049 --> 00:02:33.619
And, of course, the wealthiest
Americans are benefiting.

00:02:33.619 --> 00:02:36.255
The Trump presidency is like
an M. Night Shyamalan movie,

00:02:36.255 --> 00:02:38.591
if all the twists
are super obvious.

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:40.493
[ Laughter ]
Donald Trump would've titled
"The Sixth Sense"

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:42.161 line:0%
"Bruce Willis Is Dead."

00:02:42.161 --> 00:02:43.996 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
And, of course, some

00:02:43.996 --> 00:02:46.032
of those wealthy Americans
reaping the benefits

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:48.701
of this program include
Trump's own family.

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:51.203
-Jared Kushner is selling
his stake in a company

00:02:51.203 --> 00:02:52.505
that benefited

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:55.875 line:0%
from the tax breaks that he
personally pushed for.

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:59.411
-The Kushner family already owns
real estate on the Jersey shore,

00:02:59.411 --> 00:03:02.882
but spent an extra $13 million
in Long Branch,

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:05.718
after the area was deemed
an opportunity zone.

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:08.421
Kushner has projects
in other opportunity zones,

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:10.856
including Jersey City
and Maryland,

00:03:10.856 --> 00:03:14.226
that could get a boost in value,
all raising the question:

00:03:14.226 --> 00:03:15.794
Who really profits?

00:03:15.794 --> 00:03:18.264
-Jared Kushner?!
What a coincidence

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:21.233
that the president's son-in-law,
who works in the White House,

00:03:21.233 --> 00:03:22.568
would benefit financially.

00:03:22.568 --> 00:03:23.636
I guess he's

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:26.705
in an opportunity zone.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.705 --> 00:03:30.243
So, Jared Kushner, the moray eel
who was kissed a princess

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:32.812
and turned halfway
into a prince,

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:34.446
[ Laughter and applause ]
is making a killing.

00:03:34.446 --> 00:03:36.782
So, how? How, exactly,

00:03:36.782 --> 00:03:39.184
are the wealthy, like Kushner,
benefiting from this plan?

00:03:39.184 --> 00:03:40.653
Well, the vague language
of the law

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:44.023
leaves it up to investors
to decide what kind of projects

00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:45.224
and developments
they wanna build.

00:03:45.224 --> 00:03:47.260
There's nothing that forces them

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:48.961
to actually help
low-income communities.

00:03:48.961 --> 00:03:51.397
On top of that,
the qualifications

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:53.098
for what defines
an opportunity zone

00:03:53.098 --> 00:03:54.534
are extremely broad,

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:56.836
which defeats the very purpose
of this program.

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:59.371
-Clear pattern, so far,
is if you're an investor

00:03:59.371 --> 00:04:01.274
and you're gonna invest
in a zone,

00:04:01.274 --> 00:04:03.442
are you going to do it
in a developed city

00:04:03.442 --> 00:04:05.878 line:0%
that's already gentrified
or are you gonna do it

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:08.581 line:0%
in a truly distressed part
of the country,

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:10.149 line:0%
that is going to be a risk?

00:04:10.149 --> 00:04:11.985 line:0%
So, a lot of the money
is going to be

00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:13.519 line:0%
toward the sure investment,

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:15.688 line:0%
which, in this case,
we're already seeing is

00:04:15.688 --> 00:04:18.457 line:0%
in the highly developed,
already expensive,

00:04:18.457 --> 00:04:21.960 line:0%
high-employment parts
of the country.

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:24.496
-Some opportunity zones
have also been criticized

00:04:24.496 --> 00:04:26.799
for not being
economically distressed.

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:29.868
Almost 200 of the zones
qualified simply

00:04:29.868 --> 00:04:32.271
by being next
to low-income areas.

00:04:32.271 --> 00:04:34.173
-So the whole concept
of opportunity zones

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:36.609
sounds great, but it is
actually terrible.

00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:38.210
It's basically R. Kelly.

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:39.278
Sounds great.

00:04:39.278 --> 00:04:42.081
[ Laughter ]
Is actually terrible.

00:04:42.081 --> 00:04:43.682
[ Applause ]
And this is reportedly --

00:04:43.682 --> 00:04:45.952
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:04:45.952 --> 00:04:48.955
This is reportedly becoming
the norm for this program.

00:04:48.955 --> 00:04:50.189
According to The New York Times,

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:52.125
recent opportunity zone
projects include...

00:04:59.499 --> 00:05:01.467
[ Laughter ]
A spa for pets

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:04.537
is not the kind of thing that
helps America's inner cities.

00:05:04.537 --> 00:05:05.838
That is not what they
were crying out for.

00:05:05.838 --> 00:05:07.406
"I'm having trouble
finding work and paying rent,

00:05:07.406 --> 00:05:10.242
but the real issue is my cat
desperately needs a soft scrub."

00:05:10.242 --> 00:05:12.611
[ Laughter ]
And, because the tax benefit

00:05:12.611 --> 00:05:14.313
is lining the pockets
of the wealthy,

00:05:14.313 --> 00:05:15.815
instead of helping
low-income areas,

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:18.850
a government agency
is now investigating the program

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:20.486
and Kushner's role in it.

00:05:20.486 --> 00:05:23.222
-An internal watchdog group
with the Treasury Department

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:25.791
is taking a look into the way
the Trump administration

00:05:25.791 --> 00:05:28.294
is rolling out
opportunity zones.

00:05:28.294 --> 00:05:30.963
-The president's son-in-law,
Jared Kushner,

00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:32.999
recently announced
he was soliciting investments

00:05:32.999 --> 00:05:35.335 line:0%
in these opportunity zones,
which prompted

00:05:35.335 --> 00:05:37.270 line:0%
the Treasury Department's
inspector general

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:39.772 line:0%
to open an inquiry
into the program.

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:41.239 line:0%
-You could do good things
with this money,

00:05:41.239 --> 00:05:42.608 line:0%
if that was your mission.

00:05:42.608 --> 00:05:44.777 line:0%
Or, you could just make high-end
stuff and get a tax break,

00:05:44.777 --> 00:05:46.145 line:0%
and that's what you're
seeing with Kushner

00:05:46.145 --> 00:05:48.414 line:0%
and I'm glad the IG
is gonna look into it.

00:05:48.414 --> 00:05:50.683 line:0%
Hopefully, Trump doesn't try
to squash that.

00:05:50.683 --> 00:05:53.352
-I got a feeling that Trump
is gonna try and squash that.

00:05:53.352 --> 00:05:54.953
[ Laughter ]
If there's one thing

00:05:54.953 --> 00:05:56.889
Trump is good at,
it's squashing,

00:05:56.889 --> 00:05:59.192
whether it's investigations,
testimony,

00:05:59.192 --> 00:06:00.893
or himself into a golf cart.

00:06:00.893 --> 00:06:02.261
[ Laughter ]
I --

00:06:02.261 --> 00:06:03.729
"I don't think you're
gonna fit, sir."

00:06:03.729 --> 00:06:05.131
[as Trump]
No, I can squash.

00:06:05.131 --> 00:06:08.267
[ Laughter ]
So, despite Trump's promises,

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:10.369
opportunity zones ended up
benefiting the rich,

00:06:10.369 --> 00:06:12.371
instead of helping the poor,
so, to answer Trump's

00:06:12.371 --> 00:06:14.206
original question,
these communities have

00:06:14.206 --> 00:06:16.809
everything to lose,
if he remains in office.

00:06:16.809 --> 00:06:18.744
This has been "The Check In."

00:06:18.744 --> 00:06:20.512
[ Cheering and applause ]
♪♪

00:06:20.512 --> 00:06:22.215
